                      'Instead of relying on slow conscious logic, your brain routes the signal between the '
                      'occipital-temporal visual cortex and the superior colliculus and parietal visual pathway.',
                      'Step one: sensory signals travel from the retina through the optic nerve into the '
                      'occipital-temporal visual cortex as rapid electrical spikes.',
                      'Step two: those pulses collide inside the ventral visual recognition tract, where bilateral eye '
